@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+# Speed projection as two API model names
+
+Local patch for Strata v0.2.8 / engine 0.1.54. The Python service gives an explicitly registered
+`<model>-sp` alias a speed-projection default of `true`; the canonical model defaults to `false`.
+One loaded engine, one model's weights and the existing FIFO serve both names. The C++ engine is unchanged.
+
+The speed-projection vector must already be loaded by the engine. Register the alias through the existing
+upstream config field; no new config keys or client configuration are required:
+
+```json
+"aliases": ["qwen3.8-flash-next-iq3_xxs-sp"]
+```
+
+API model names:
+
+| `model` | Default `experimental_speed_projection` |
+| --- | --- |
+| `qwen3.8-flash-next-iq3_xxs` | `false` |
+| `qwen3.8-flash-next-iq3_xxs-sp` | `true` |
+
+The convention is opt-in: without that registered alias, existing behavior stays unchanged. Other aliases
+keep the upstream behavior. `/v1/models` and `/models` list both names with their existing context and modality
+metadata, plus `default_parameters.experimental_speed_projection` for these presets.
+
+Precedence is an explicit request field, then the named model's projection preset, then existing global defaults.
+Thus `experimental_speed_projection: false` explicitly sent with the `-sp` model still turns projection off,
+and the existing web switch continues working. Selecting the model name alone is sufficient when the client
+omits the projection field. No request changes global settings or starts another engine.
+
+OpenAI Chat Completions, OpenAI Responses and Anthropic Messages use the same sampling merge. Responses streaming
+also keeps the selected model name. Current-session prefix reuse works within each projection mode. Switching
+projection modes invalidates the existing KV/checkpoints through the upstream engine's existing checks; the two
+modes must not share KV computed under different projection states. Parking remains independently configurable.
+
+Apply and check from the source checkout:
+
+```sh
+git apply --check /opt/strata/local-patches/0003-api-projection-models.patch
+git apply /opt/strata/local-patches/0003-api-projection-models.patch
+python3.14 -m unittest tests.terminal.test_projection_model_alias -v
+sudo systemctl restart strata.service
+```
+
+The local deployment uses 262144 context, INT8 KV streaming with resident window 32768, parking off, automatic
+ROUTE_PRIOR, and Codex title bypass. This patch does not change those choices or any Codex settings. No CUDA build
+is needed for this Python-only patch. On future updates, run `git apply --check` and review conflicts; do not force
+an old patch onto changed sampling code. To remove, reverse this patch and remove the `-sp` entry from `aliases`.
+
+Related upstream proposals: [issue #4048](https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/issues/4048) and
+[PR #4050](https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/pull/4050). This focused patch uses the existing alias list and covers
+Responses as well as chat and messages. It has not been submitted upstream.
